# The whole @fsarch scope comes from GitHub Packages: the service packages are
# only published there, and registries can only be mapped per scope, so
# @fsarch/server is resolved from there as well (it's published to both).
#
# The auth token deliberately isn't configured here: pnpm ignores registry
# credentials from a repository-controlled .npmrc. It has to come from the
# user-level ~/.npmrc instead (`//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<token with
# read:packages>`, e.g. `gh auth token`) - the Docker build gets it the same
# way, as a secret file mounted at /root/.npmrc (see Dockerfile).
@fsarch:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
